course: dictionary
lesson: 9719
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Summit can mean the top of a mountain, or a meeting of leaders. The words around it give you the clue.
explain: «The summit of Chimborazo in Ecuador is the point on Earth farthest from the planet's centre.» The words Chimborazo, Earth and point tell you this summit is a mountain top. Ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Summit can also be a verb, a word for doing something. «The climbers hoped to summit before lunch» means they hoped to reach the top. When a word changes its job in a sentence, its meaning can change too.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Summit» means the highest point or top of a mountain or hill.
fact: A «summit» can also be an important meeting between leaders of countries, called a summit meeting.
fact: The summit of something is its highest level or greatest success.
fact: As a verb, «summit» means to reach the top of a mountain.
exercise: «The summit of Chimborazo in Ecuador is the point on Earth farthest from the planet's centre.» What does summit mean here? | The lowest point under the sea | *The highest point of a mountain | A long walk home | A meeting between leaders
exercise: Leaders met for a «summit meeting» to talk about peace. What does summit mean here? | A climb to the top of a hill | *A meeting between leaders of countries | The top of a mountain | A map with a spot height
exercise: The climbers hoped to ____ the mountain before lunch. Which word fits best? | summon | summer | sundae | *summit
test: «Her summit of success came when she won the national prize.» What does summit mean here? | The top of a hill she climbed | A meeting with the prize judges | A slow walk home | *Her highest level or greatest success
test: In «They want to summit Everest in May», what kind of word is summit, and what does it mean? | *A verb, meaning to reach the top | A noun, meaning a map mark | An adjective, meaning very high | A noun, meaning a meeting
exam: In the news, «a summit in Geneva» most likely means | A climber's rope | A spot height on a map | *A meeting of world leaders | The top of a volcano
